1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:01,950
A punch lands in the ring.

2
00:00:05,020 --> 00:00:05,970
On the broadcast,

3
00:00:06,300 --> 00:00:08,270
that punch lands five seconds later.

4
00:00:10,420 --> 00:00:11,710
In those five seconds,

5
00:00:11,760 --> 00:00:13,570
anyone watching faster already knows

6
00:00:13,420 --> 00:00:14,390
the price is wrong.

7
00:00:15,980 --> 00:00:17,650
Sportsbooks call it courtsiding,

8
00:00:17,920 --> 00:00:19,270
and they answer it by freezing

9
00:00:19,120 --> 00:00:19,790
the market.

10
00:00:21,540 --> 00:00:23,250
Ringside answers it with the clock.

11
00:00:25,700 --> 00:00:27,870
Ringside is an in-play fight exchange

12
00:00:27,720 --> 00:00:28,590
on Solana.

13
00:00:28,440 --> 00:00:30,290
The fight and the order book

14
00:00:30,140 --> 00:00:33,050
run inside the same MagicBlock ephemeral rollup,

15
00:00:33,240 --> 00:00:34,150
ten ticks a second.

16
00:00:35,080 --> 00:00:36,650
Every order is stamped with the

17
00:00:36,500 --> 00:00:37,850
tick it was priced on.

18
00:00:38,020 --> 00:00:39,350
If the fight has moved on,

19
00:00:39,520 --> 00:00:41,010
the program refuses the order.

20
00:00:42,340 --> 00:00:44,030
Here is a real devnet match,

21
00:00:44,040 --> 00:00:45,110
at its biggest hit.

22
00:00:45,480 --> 00:00:46,150
Red lands,

23
00:00:46,420 --> 00:00:47,850
and the fair price jumps in

24
00:00:47,700 --> 00:00:48,470
the same tick.

25
00:00:49,580 --> 00:00:51,550
A bot watching the five-second TV

26
00:00:51,400 --> 00:00:52,850
feed sends the old price.

27
00:00:53,220 --> 00:00:54,250
On a delayed book,

28
00:00:54,280 --> 00:00:54,850
it fills.

29
00:00:55,160 --> 00:00:55,930
On Ringside,

30
00:00:55,880 --> 00:00:57,730
the same order is rejected onchain.

31
00:00:58,940 --> 00:01:00,910
Tonight's card lists every live bout.

32
00:01:01,060 --> 00:01:01,730
AI fighters,

33
00:01:01,800 --> 00:01:02,890
trained by self-play,

34
00:01:03,060 --> 00:01:04,450
run in the lobby around the clock,

35
00:01:04,500 --> 00:01:05,770
and you can challenge one yourself.

36
00:01:07,340 --> 00:01:08,050
Inside a match,

37
00:01:08,240 --> 00:01:09,790
the odds move with every hit.

38
00:01:10,060 --> 00:01:11,550
In a load test of 8 bots,

39
00:01:11,900 --> 00:01:14,370
fills confirmed in 262 milliseconds

40
00:01:14,220 --> 00:01:15,170
at the median.

41
00:01:16,580 --> 00:01:18,150
Positions live in a private rollup

42
00:01:18,000 --> 00:01:19,890
inside a TEE.

43
00:01:20,280 --> 00:01:21,970
Nobody else can read yours until

44
00:01:21,820 --> 00:01:22,310
the bell.

45
00:01:23,140 --> 00:01:24,210
At the bell,

46
00:01:24,540 --> 00:01:25,730
settlement pays the winner,

47
00:01:25,880 --> 00:01:27,070
reveals every position,

48
00:01:27,300 --> 00:01:29,290
and writes the match record to Solana.

49
00:01:30,480 --> 00:01:31,790
Then anyone can replay the match

50
00:01:31,640 --> 00:01:32,430
in their browser.

51
00:01:32,820 --> 00:01:33,530
Press verify,

52
00:01:33,880 --> 00:01:35,410
and it re-runs every tick and

53
00:01:35,260 --> 00:01:37,070
checks the hash chain written onchain.

54
00:01:37,980 --> 00:01:38,650
Under the hood,

55
00:01:38,960 --> 00:01:40,390
the fight and the book are

56
00:01:40,240 --> 00:01:41,770
one ephemeral rollup,

57
00:01:41,920 --> 00:01:43,510
cranked every hundred milliseconds.

58
00:01:44,820 --> 00:01:47,010
MagicBlock VRF seeds the power-ups.

59
00:01:47,440 --> 00:01:48,610
Session keys sign every move.

60
00:01:48,460 --> 00:01:50,770
The private rollup seals each position.

61
00:01:50,980 --> 00:01:52,610
And Magic Actions write the result

62
00:01:52,460 --> 00:01:53,390
back to Solana.

63
00:01:54,700 --> 00:01:56,210
We measured it on devnet.

64
00:01:56,480 --> 00:01:58,290
Across 23 held-out matches,

65
00:01:58,580 --> 00:02:01,450
the delayed book accepted 319 stale fills.

66
00:02:01,860 --> 00:02:03,150
Ringside accepted zero,

67
00:02:03,440 --> 00:02:06,230
and rejected 1,283 stale orders onchain.

68
00:02:07,500 --> 00:02:09,270
Ticks landed every 100 milliseconds

69
00:02:09,120 --> 00:02:10,030
at the median.

70
00:02:10,500 --> 00:02:12,770
60 of 60 private reads were denied.

71
00:02:12,980 --> 00:02:15,570
And 19 of 19 replays verified,

72
00:02:15,420 --> 00:02:17,990
10,266 ticks checked.

73
00:02:18,680 --> 00:02:20,030
A punch lands,

74
00:02:20,360 --> 00:02:21,610
and the price moves in the

75
00:02:21,460 --> 00:02:22,270
same instruction.

76
00:02:22,760 --> 00:02:24,390
There is no gap left to trade.

77
00:02:25,380 --> 00:02:26,090
Ringside.

78
00:02:26,400 --> 00:02:27,470
Live on devnet,

79
00:02:27,500 --> 00:02:28,150
open source,

80
00:02:28,280 --> 00:02:29,470
and ready for the next fight.

